run the simulation indicated in @docs/06-agent-architecture.md. focus specifically on the following case.

  FIRST, read @CASE-BASELINE.md — it is the canonical, current description of this
  case (Era B, from 2026-08-02) and it supersedes the case framing embedded in
  protocol-v1..v4, sims/01-09, docs/, and ADR-0001..0020. Those artifacts are
  preserved, not rewritten; CASE-BASELINE.md §5 is the translation table for
  reading them, including the fact that this case now has NO P0 anchor on the
  evidence-transferability ladder (ADR-0014) and Directness must be
  posterior-weighted across driver hypotheses.

  === PATIENT CASE ===
  Small round-cell sarcoma, clinically and histologically CIC-like / EWING-LIKE,
  diagnosed June 2024, WITHOUT a confirming fusion match on genome sequencing —
  i.e. the ~5% genomically-uncharacterized atypical subgroup (no confirmed
  CIC-DUX4/CIC-NUTM1/CIC-FOXO4). THE DRIVER IS UNRESOLVED. Any recommendation
  that depends on the fusion being present (e.g. junction ASOs, junction-specific
  neoantigen vaccines, the MCL1 "re-arm the DUX4 death program" line) must be
  flagged as possibly inapplicable to this patient and held as driver-contingent.

  Do NOT default to canonical CIC-DUX4 biology. Current driver posterior
  (sims/10-chemoresponse-cellstate/): D4 phenocopy/misclassified 0.386 >
  D1 cryptic CIC-DUX4 0.264 > D5 orphan 0.156 > D2 rare partner 0.100 >
  D3 non-fusion CIC LOF 0.095.
  Equally: do NOT overclaim the reverse. "Not CIC-DUX4" is NOT established —
  cryptic CIC-DUX4 still holds ~26%, and "Ewing-like" is a morphological
  descriptor covering several entities, not a molecular diagnosis. No EWSR1
  fusion has been reported either.

  === CHEMOTHERAPY RESPONSE (treat as EVIDENCE, not just history) ===
  This tumour has now shown a deep response to conventional chemotherapy TWICE:
  >95% necrosis at first-line resection, and a COMPLETE radiographic response of
  relapsed lung nodules after 4 cycles of ifosfamide. That is atypical for
  canonical CIC-DUX4 (repair-proficient/POLE-high; only ~30% respond well) and
  matches the Ewing/round-cell family instead. Per ADR-0021 it implies a
  cycling, apoptotically-primed, repair-limited (predicted SLFN11-competent)
  cell state — resolved to ~94% posterior — and it means the unsolved problem
  is the persister RESERVOIR, not the chemo-sensitive bulk. Caveat honestly:
  the response is confounded with setting (burden, lesion size, dose intensity),
  and the relapse CR is radiographic, not pathologic, in a post-WLI lung.

  - Primary tumor site: biceps femoris of the right thigh.
  - At diagnosis: 12 nodules of metastases across both lungs.
  - Treatment: EURO EWING protocol (VDC/IE backbone — vincristine, doxorubicin,
    cyclophosphamide, ifosfamide, etoposide), 14 cycles, good chemo response.
    All lung metastases were destroyed; the primary tumor was calcified and
    >95% of cells were dead at the time of surgery.
  - Surgery January 2025: tumor removed along with the (biceps femoris) muscle.
  - After chemotherapy: radiation therapy to the leg AND to both lungs
    (whole-lung irradiation).
  - NED (no evidence of disease) from May 2025 until May 2026.
  - May 2026: a single cluster of metastases discovered on ONE lung
    (oligometastatic relapse after ~1 year NED).
  - Relapse treatment: HIGH-DOSE IFOSFAMIDE. After 4 cycles the lung nodules
    have DISAPPEARED on imaging (complete radiographic response).
  - CURRENT STATE: minimal residual disease / complete radiographic response
    following chemotherapy. This is the second deep response this tumour has
    produced. Note the timing consequence (ADR-0021): the post-chemotherapy
    window — lowest tumour burden + lymphodepletion rebound + synchronous
    antigen release, on top of the earlier whole-lung irradiation — is the
    best immunological moment this patient has had, and it CLOSES on its own.

  === PATIENT'S SELF-ADMINISTERED NATURAL REGIMEN (must be assessed explicitly) ===
  During the first EURO EWING course, in the rest weeks between VDC/IE cycles
  (i.e. when not receiving chemo), the patient alternated chemo with natural
  medicine:
    - curcumin (curcuma) + piperine
    - liposomal vitamin C
    - black cumin seed oil (Nigella sativa / thymoquinone)
    - vitamin D
    - honey
    - fresh juice of celery, ginger, carrot, broccoli, apple, and beetroot
  During the year of NED the patient continued curcumin + piperine,
  liposomal vitamin C, black cumin seed oil, vitamin D, and honey.

  Do not merely catalogue these — have the relevant vectors evaluate this actual
  regimen as helping / neutral / potentially harmful, and address the drug
  interactions head-on, especially:
    - piperine as a CYP3A4 / P-gp inhibitor versus the
      ifosfamide prodrug (now imminent) and vincristine/etoposide/doxorubicin;
      include the Shoba 1998 caveat for the bioavailability claim
    - high-dose antioxidants (liposomal vitamin C) during ROS-dependent chemo
      (doxorubicin, ifosfamide)
    - β-carotene from carrot juice and the ATBC/CARET harm signal
    - sulforaphane from broccoli (myrosinase activity / effect of juicing)
    - thymoquinone, apigenin/luteolin (celery), 6-gingerol (ginger),
      quercetin (apple), and nitrate (beetroot) as candidate bioactive effectors
  The Orchestrator's final output should carry a dedicated
  "Patient's Actual Self-Administered Regimen" section.

  === OUTPUT REQUIREMENT ===
  In the final output, clearly state at the top — as a key-map callout — what
  each vector represents, so a later reader knows what V1, V2, V3, and V4
  mean.

  Do not use any memory stored about the patient — this has to be a clean-slate
  research exercise.
